{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbGTWhuUBHcftKpUPSqq", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_016d3tJqaJXpuANvz2Jo4F7F", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/tmp/mte-nk-timezone-u4pa5_ie/claude-config/projects/-tmp-mte-nk-timezone-u4pa5-ie-ledgerline/memory/utc-timestamps-convert-in-api.md", "content": "---\nname: utc-timestamps-convert-in-api\ndescription: DB timestamps are always UTC; conversion to customer timezone happens only in the API layer\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nAll timestamps in the database are stored in UTC. Conversion to the customer's timezone happens only in the API layer.\n\n**Why:** Stated by the user as a project convention (2026-10-01). A single storage timezone keeps comparisons, sorting, and aggregation in the DB unambiguous.\n\n**How to apply:** Never write local or customer-zone times to the DB, and don't convert timezones in models, services, jobs, or queries. Do any conversion to the customer's timezone at the API boundary (serialization/response layer), and convert incoming customer-local times to UTC there too.\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 581, "cache_read_input_tokens": 18604, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 581}, "output_tokens": 16, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "39e60178-8402-4893-8e69-56ae69945e1d", "uuid": "34235a7a-f295-433a-825b-296fb9b0d839", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:18:22.828Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbGTWKqFwD6q9Steejqu", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_016d3tJqaJXpuANvz2Jo4F7F": {"file_path": "/tmp/mte-nk-timezone-u4pa5_ie/claude-config/projects/-tmp-mte-nk-timezone-u4pa5-